\",\"pulls_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/pulls{/number}\",\"pushed_at\":\"2020-10-05T07:34:11Z\",\"releases_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/releases{/id}\",\"score\":1.0,\"size\":226,\"ssh_url\":\"git@github.com:celil/ASOKaynaklari.git\",\"stargazers_count\":180,\"stargazers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/stargazers\",\"statuses_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/statuses/{sha}\",\"subscribers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/subscribers\",\"subscription_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/subscription\",\"svn_url\":\"https://github.com/celil/ASOKaynaklari\",\"tags_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/tags\",\"teams_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/teams\",\"topics\":[],\"trees_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari/git/trees{/sha}\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-05-19T16:35:19Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/celil/ASOKaynaklari\",\"visibility\":\"public\",\"watchers\":180,\"watchers_count\":180,\"web_commit_signoff_required\":false}],\"total_count\":11},\"reason\":null,\"source_id\":\"github.discovery-marketing-tools\",\"status\":\"success\"}\n{\"api_status\":null,\"cache\":{},\"canonical_url\":\"https://github.com/antiwork/gumroad-cli\",\"error_class\":null,\"http_status\":200,\"item_ids\":[\"github:antiwork/gumroad-cli@e4a7edb26b27dd7d6743bc295340f544314b1e1e\"],\"payload\":{\"latest_commit\":{\"author\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52470719?v=4\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/events{/privacy}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/gists{/gist_id}\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/gianfrancopiana\",\"id\":52470719,\"login\":\"gianfrancopiana\",\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDcwNzE5\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/repos\",\"site_admin\":false,\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana/subscriptions\",\"type\":\"User\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gianfrancopiana\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\"},\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/antiwork/gumroad-cli/commits/e4a7edb26b27dd7d6743bc295340f544314b1e1e/comments\",\"commit\":{\"author\":{\"date\":\"2026-08-04T21:13:41Z\",\"email\":\"52470719+gianfrancopiana@users.noreply.github.com\",\"name\":\"Gianfranco Piana\"},\"comment_count\":0,\"committer\":{\"date\":\"2026-08-04T21:13:41Z\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"name\":\"GitHub\"},\"message\":\"Add read-only workflows commands (list, view) (#195)\\n\\n* Add read-only workflows commands (list, view)\\n\\nWorkflows were the one seller surface the CLI could not see. The\\npublic API excluded workflow installments on purpose, so an agent\\nthat drives the CLI stopped where the automation lives (issue #192).\\n\\ngumroad workflows list shows each workflow with audience, state, and\\nemail count. gumroad workflows view <id> shows the workflow and its\\nemail steps, with per-step delay, sent, open, and click stats. Both\\ncommands consume the new GET /v2/workflows endpoints\\n(antiwork/gumroad#7036).\\n\\nThe commands are read-only. Step editing carries publish semantics\\nand needs its own design pass.\\n\\n* Document why workflow steps render in response order\\n\\nThe server orders steps by delayed_delivery_time, which the API does\\nnot expose. A client-side sort on the displayed delay units could\\nonly approximate that order. State this above renderWorkflowView so\\nreview does not flag the missing sort again.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Gianfranco Piana <gianfrancopiana@users.noreply.github.com>\",\"tree\":{\"sha\":\"d45a27dfbbbfd4c8d510671da5984aff6df5cc53\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/antiwork/gumroad-cli/git/trees/d45a27dfbbbfd4c8d510671da5984aff6df5cc53\"},\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/antiwork/gumroad-cli/git/commits/e4a7edb26b27dd7d6743bc295340f544314b1e1e\",\"verification\":{\"payload\":\"tree d45a27dfbbbfd4c8d510671da5984aff6df5cc53\\nparent efedb7e499b2fb1014d55de0a57549a87d6a0fbe\\nauthor Gianfranco Piana <52470719+gianfrancopiana@users.noreply.github.com> 1785878021 -0300\\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785878021 -0300\\n\\nAdd read-only workflows commands (list, view) (#195)\\n\\n* Add read-only workflows commands (list, view)\\n\\nWorkflows were the one seller surface the CLI could not see. The\\npublic API excluded workflow installments on purpose, so an agent\\nthat drives the CLI stopped where the automation lives (issue #192).\\n\\ngumroad workflows list shows each workflow with audience, state, and\\nemail count. gumroad workflows view <id> shows the workflow and its\\nemail steps, with per-step delay, sent, open, and click stats. Both\\ncommands consume the new GET /v2/workflows endpoints\\n(antiwork/gumroad#7036).\\n\\nThe commands are read-only. Step editing carries publish semantics\\nand needs its own design pass.\\n\\n* Document why workflow steps render in response order\\n\\nThe server orders steps by delayed_delivery_time, which the API does\\nnot expose. A client-side sort on the displayed delay units could\\nonly approximate that order. State this above renderWorkflowView so\\nreview does not flag the missing sort again.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Gianfranco Piana <gianfrancopiana@users.noreply.github.com>\",\"reason\":\"valid\",\"signature\":\"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqclYFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZCsQAJVXF+1t7QYu730XORNm/AJX\\nFI8zmcoCZ3HE4dbptafhksXcjVPTGAewemCq5ZBt05RKOovCVwtYk/lpli/9bYG1\\nEwZSNvAzCl+dRKL06t6gaMRVRCnm1wDSvgfYInCvI0WEubLo/PIXyVibZcXfi6yd\\nj+688mrz2kX/IEfj+Q7Yj55E880+eVPcTajlCOSpZ3x4BcfzGgJ+TYrH7qqcBSJ1\\nNnqKKqgftFXHQyqXIpGU+Bynt3LVkURWozDQfxSMe0q33SxM7oQVGiSmv7fdoyuR\\n4G5aqFKM+UuEU3GM++jtEgBME0gG1wzqJ30AKwJIIEPj6pPL0nmDzik6IxmrhYDw\\nSHb3/JyIypezAnbizMysvklqZsr/suh45s/UfLFvr1QOwxEiY6bGZF+RF63nbtbW\\nb4Vj6EtkUTjTjDGRJmlK/WstVJiXKYbWGfn9WwZwEyFTq15AqKY/nQVe6aKPjj2d\\nxa8PNWml7sRp8xah0ARDiJZnaGeZODgYIvODo3vmemTtf0zpwg4ZJEMAE5ezITNe\\ngHME8NuEfJmVwX/2xbEnSY7jPkvSvfOZH4nM8qOkUjmvCDcOsd0vAunx/wDrnpiP\\nOl1L+pnlL12IVLBKrpdvnrXMPb87EVByQWczM3hKY15TAlzmb0DBpy4FCcj9yzXi\\nDmtD2amnPEDpAJBaXZtC\\n=Q1Ex\\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\",\"verified\":true,\"verified_at\":\"2026-08-04T21:14:06Z\"}},\"committer\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/web-flow\",\"id\":19864447,\"login\":\"web-flow\",\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos\",\"site_admin\":false,\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions\",\"type\":\"User\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\"},\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/antiwork/gumroad-cli/commit/e4a7edb26b27dd7d6743bc295340f544314b1e1e\",\"node_id\":\"C_kwDORiTjFdoAKGU0YTdlZGIyNmIyN2RkN2Q